+# Gamma resolve shader sources
+
+BSD-licensed Xenia Canary sources from
+`534aeb64ea1937361573e3933d121e636463b135` (original notices retained).
+Includes are flattened into this directory. The gamma-only source format is specialized without changing push constants.
+Non-gamma resolves retain the original SDK bytecodes. The scalar algorithm is
+unchanged: decode to 10-bit codes, average, PWL quantize, normalize, exp_bias;
+alpha remains fixed.
+
+Adaptations preserve the pinned ReXGlue ABI and consumers:
+- EDRAM sample bits use the existing SDK vertical/horizontal arrangement.
+- Scaled destinations retain 8-byte R8 and 16-byte other-format blocks.
+- Second stores in scaled 64/128bpp kernels calculate their own block address.
+- FXC IEEE strictness and precise unpack/accumulation prevent alpha reassociation.
+- Sample-address reuse from 3989ba3 is excluded pending numerical/GPU measurement.
+
+All 20 DXBC/SPIR-V headers are shipped. Normal Release builds need no shader
+compiler or downloads. Regeneration is maintenance-only, from the project root:
+
+```bat
+scripts\devshell.cmd cmake --build --preset win-amd64-release --target x360n_resolve_shader_compiler
+scripts\devshell.cmd .local\toolchains\python-3.14.8\python.exe scripts\shaders\generate_resolves.py --sdk-root external/rexglue-sdk --fxc <Windows-SDK-fxc.exe> --spirv-compiler .local/build/win-amd64/tests/sdkcheck/g3/Release/x360n_resolve_shader_compiler.exe --spirv-tools <SPIRV-Tools-bin>
+```
+
+Use `--verify` to compare exact regenerated resources. `generated.json` records
+source, compiler and binary hashes. SPIRV-Tools can be built offline from
+`thirdparty/spirv-tools` with `SPIRV-Headers_SOURCE_DIR` pointing at
+`thirdparty/spirv-headers`, `SPIRV_SKIP_TESTS=ON`, using `scripts/devshell.cmd`.
+The generator validates every Vulkan module for Vulkan 1.0 and preserves
+bindings and the 20-byte (16-byte scaled) push-constant interface.
